===============================================================================
Attachment A

USE RESTRICTIONS
===============================================================================

You agree not to use the Data or Derivatives of the Data:

General

- In any way that violates any applicable national, federal, state, local or
  international law or regulation, or in violation of the terms of the EMSCAD
  corpus from which the annotated sentences are drawn;
- For the purpose of exploiting, harming or attempting to exploit or harm minors in
  any way;
- To generate or disseminate verifiably false information and/or content with the
  purpose of harming others;
- To generate or disseminate personal identifiable information that can be used to
  harm an individual;
- To defame, disparage or otherwise harass others;
- To exploit any of the vulnerabilities of a specific group of persons based on
  their age, social, physical or mental characteristics, in order to materially
  distort the behavior of a person pertaining to that group in a manner that causes
  or is likely to cause that person or another person physical or psychological
  harm;
- For any use intended to or which has the effect of discriminating against or
  harming individuals or groups based on online or offline social behavior or known
  or predicted personal or personality characteristics;
- For any use intended to or which has the effect of discriminating against
  individuals or groups based on legally protected characteristics or categories.

Employment and recruitment

- To make, inform, automate or materially assist any decision about an identified or
  identifiable person, including screening, ranking, scoring, shortlisting,
  rejecting, promoting, or setting the terms of employment. The Data describes
  properties of text. It says nothing about a candidate, and it must not be made to;
- For fully automated decision making that adversely impacts an individual's legal
  rights or otherwise creates or modifies a binding, enforceable obligation;
- To compose, tune or test recruitment language whose purpose or effect is to deter
  or exclude applicants on the basis of a protected attribute, including inverting
  the Data or any Derivative of the Data to discover wording that evades bias
  detection while preserving its exclusionary effect;
- To infer, impute or predict a protected attribute of any individual, whether an
  applicant, an employee, or the author of an advertisement;
- To deploy in any setting affecting a person's access to employment without
  meaningful human review of each flagged span, and without disclosing to affected
  parties that an automated tool is in use.

Representation of results

- To represent an Output as a legal determination of discrimination, as a compliance
  certification, or as evidence of an employer's intent;
- To represent an Output as establishing the presence of bias without disclosing the
  measured reliability of the relevant category, including the low inter-annotator
  agreement of the implicit ("Coded") categories and the exploratory status of the
  Old Coded and Young Coded categories.

Annotators

- To attempt to re-identify any annotator who contributed to the Data, or to link
  the pseudonymous annotator identifiers to any external record.

These restrictions apply to You and to everyone You Distribute to. Any license You
grant downstream must carry them forward unchanged.
